### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### BluestoneX Expense — runnable OData V4 request collection
###
### Run against a local server:  cds watch    (base = http://localhost:4004)
### Tooling: VS Code "REST Client" or JetBrains .http runner.
### Each request notes its EXPECTED status. `###` separates requests; `# @name`
### captures a response so later requests can reuse values (id / csrf token).
###
### Auth: HTTP Basic. REST Client encodes `Basic <user> <pass>` for you.
### Mock users (dev): full email is the username.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@host = http://localhost:4004
@emp  = sabarinathan.chandrasekar@bluestonex.com sab
@mgr  = manager@bluestonex.com mgr
@dan  = Dan.Barton@bluestonex.com dan
@in1  = suresh.rajarathinam@bluestonex.com suresh
@clerk = clerk@bluestonex.com clerk
@priya = priya.sharma@bluestonex.com priya

### 1. $metadata — EXPECT 200, XML with EntitySet "MyClaims" + Action "submitClaim"
GET {{host}}/expense/$metadata
Authorization: Basic {{emp}}

### 2. CSRF: fetch a token (needed for the manual receipt PUT) — EXPECT 200 + x-csrf-token header
# @name csrf
HEAD {{host}}/expense/
Authorization: Basic {{emp}}
x-csrf-token: Fetch

### 3. Create a draft claim (UK) — EXPECT 201; capture the new ID
# @name newClaim
POST {{host}}/expense/MyClaims
Authorization: Basic {{emp}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "country": "UK", "claimPeriod": "2026-02-28" }

### 4. Add an expense item to the draft — EXPECT 201
POST {{host}}/expense/MyClaims(ID={{newClaim.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=false)/items
Authorization: Basic {{emp}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expenseDate": "2026-02-16", "expenseType_code": "HOTEL", "reasonForTrip": "Client visit", "vatType": "STD", "grossAmount": 120, "receiptAttached": true }

### 5. Activate the draft (draftActivate) — EXPECT 200/201; server computes net=100, VAT=20
POST {{host}}/expense/MyClaims(ID={{newClaim.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=false)/ExpenseService.draftActivate
Authorization: Basic {{emp}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 6. Read back with $expand=items — EXPECT 200; items[0].netAmount=100, vatAmount=20
GET {{host}}/expense/MyClaims(ID={{newClaim.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=true)?$expand=items
Authorization: Basic {{emp}}

### 7. Submit for approval (submitClaim) — EXPECT 200 (status → Submitted)
POST {{host}}/expense/MyClaims(ID={{newClaim.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=true)/ExpenseService.submitClaim
Authorization: Basic {{emp}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 8. Approve as the WRONG person (sab, not configured L1) — EXPECT 403
POST {{host}}/approval/Approvals({{newClaim.response.body.ID}})/ApprovalService.approve
Authorization: Basic {{emp}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "comment": "should be blocked" }

### 9. Approve as the configured UK L1 (manager) — EXPECT 200 (status → FirstApproved)
POST {{host}}/approval/Approvals({{newClaim.response.body.ID}})/ApprovalService.approve
Authorization: Basic {{mgr}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "comment": "L1 ok" }

### 10. Approve as UK L2 (Dan) — EXPECT 200 (status → Approved)
POST {{host}}/approval/Approvals({{newClaim.response.body.ID}})/ApprovalService.approve
Authorization: Basic {{dan}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "comment": "L2 ok" }

### ─── Query options ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 11. $filter eq — EXPECT 200, exactly the UK row
GET {{host}}/expense/Countries?$filter=code eq 'UK'
Authorization: Basic {{emp}}

### 12. $top + $count — EXPECT 200, value.length=2, @odata.count=10
GET {{host}}/expense/ExpenseTypes?$top=2&$count=true
Authorization: Basic {{emp}}

### 13. $orderby desc — EXPECT 200, codes sorted descending
GET {{host}}/expense/ExpenseTypes?$orderby=code desc
Authorization: Basic {{emp}}

### ─── Negative / security ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 14. Unauthenticated — EXPECT 401
GET {{host}}/expense/MyClaims

### 15. Employee-only user hitting the approvals queue — EXPECT 403
GET {{host}}/approval/Approvals
Authorization: Basic {{priya}}

### 16. CSRF NEGATIVE: state-changing POST WITHOUT a token — EXPECT 403
###     (Meaningful only against the approuter/deployed server or `cds watch`
###      with a cookie session; stateless basic-auth may relax this.)
POST {{host}}/expense/MyClaims
Authorization: Basic {{emp}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "country": "UK", "claimPeriod": "2026-02-28" }

### 17. BYPASS D10 — employee reads line items directly — EXPECT (secure) 403/empty; ACTUAL today: 200 with rows
GET {{host}}/expense/MyClaimItems
Authorization: Basic {{priya}}

### 18. BYPASS D9 — employee reads all approval line items — EXPECT (secure) 403; ACTUAL today: 200 with rows
GET {{host}}/approval/ApprovalItems
Authorization: Basic {{priya}}

### 19. Invalid $filter (unknown property) — EXPECT 400
GET {{host}}/expense/Countries?$filter=nosuchprop eq 1
Authorization: Basic {{emp}}

### 20. GET a non-existent key — EXPECT 404
GET {{host}}/expense/MyClaims(ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000,IsActiveEntity=true)
Authorization: Basic {{emp}}

### 21. PDF export as approver — EXPECT 200, base64 body starting %PDF- ; as employee-only EXPECT 403
GET {{host}}/approval/exportClaimsPdf(scope='history',status=null,country=null,claimNo=null,fromDate=null,toDate=null)
Authorization: Basic {{mgr}}

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### GAP COVERAGE — draft-lock self-heal, SoD, malformed paging, media, analytics
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 22. Create a draft claim (UK) — EXPECT 201  (capture id for the self-heal flow)
# @name gapDraft
POST {{host}}/expense/MyClaims
Authorization: Basic {{emp}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "country": "UK", "claimPeriod": "2026-02-28" }

### 22b. Add a valid item (TOLLS £10, no receipt needed) — EXPECT 201
POST {{host}}/expense/MyClaims(ID={{gapDraft.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=false)/items
Authorization: Basic {{emp}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expenseDate": "2026-02-16", "expenseType_code": "TOLLS", "reasonForTrip": "Toll", "vatType": "STD", "grossAmount": 10 }

### 22c. Activate (save) — EXPECT 201
POST {{host}}/expense/MyClaims(ID={{gapDraft.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=false)/ExpenseService.draftActivate
Authorization: Basic {{emp}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 22d. Edit → strands a sibling draft + CAP lock — EXPECT 201
POST {{host}}/expense/MyClaims(ID={{gapDraft.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=true)/ExpenseService.draftEdit
Authorization: Basic {{emp}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "PreserveChanges": true }

### 22e. SELF-HEAL: activate the stranded draft (releases the lock) — EXPECT 200
POST {{host}}/expense/MyClaims(ID={{gapDraft.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=false)/ExpenseService.draftActivate
Authorization: Basic {{emp}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 22f. Submit the active claim — EXPECT 200, status "Submitted"  (on HANA the pre-heal submit would 409)
POST {{host}}/expense/MyClaims(ID={{gapDraft.response.body.ID}},IsActiveEntity=true)/ExpenseService.submitClaim
Authorization: Basic {{emp}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 23. SEPARATION OF DUTIES — the configured UK L1 approver (manager) submits a claim, then
### tries to approve it. Create+submit as MANAGER, then approve as MANAGER — EXPECT 403 "own".
# @name sodClaim
POST {{host}}/expense/MyClaims
Authorization: Basic {{mgr}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "country": "UK", "claimPeriod": "2026-02-28" }

### 23b. add item + activate + submit as MANAGER (run each; abbreviated here) then:
POST {{host}}/approval/Approvals({{sodClaim.response.body.ID}})/ApprovalService.approve
Authorization: Basic {{mgr}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "comment": "self-approve attempt — EXPECT 403" }

### 24. Malformed $top — EXPECT 400
GET {{host}}/expense/ExpenseTypes?$top=-1
Authorization: Basic {{emp}}

### 25. Malformed $skip — EXPECT 400
GET {{host}}/expense/ExpenseTypes?$skip=abc
Authorization: Basic {{emp}}

### 26. claimJourney with empty arg — EXPECT 400
GET {{host}}/approval/claimJourney(claimNumber='')
Authorization: Basic {{mgr}}

### 27. claimJourney unknown claim — EXPECT 404
GET {{host}}/approval/claimJourney(claimNumber='NOPE-9999')
Authorization: Basic {{mgr}}

### 28. exportClaimsPdf with a filter that matches nothing — EXPECT 200 (empty but valid PDF)
GET {{host}}/approval/exportClaimsPdf(scope='approvals',status=null,country=null,claimNo='NOPE-9999',fromDate=null,toDate=null)
Authorization: Basic {{mgr}}

### 29. dashboardStats — EXPECT 200, counts {UK,IN,total}; as employee-only EXPECT 403
GET {{host}}/approval/dashboardStats(fromDate=null,toDate=null,country=null)
Authorization: Basic {{mgr}}
